course: dictionary
lesson: 11598
title: Appease: calming and giving in
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To appease someone is to calm them down by giving them what they want. «Dad gave the crying toddler a biscuit to appease him.» The toddler wanted the biscuit, and once he had it, he stopped crying. So appease means calm someone by giving them what they want.
explain: Appease can also mean giving in too easily. «Sam kept whining about the TV, so his sister let him choose the film just to appease him.» She did not really want to, but she gave in so that he would stop. The clue is the word just: she gave in to keep the peace.
explain: In history, appease means giving in to an aggressive country's demands to avoid war. Before the Second World War, some leaders tried to appease Hitler, hoping to stop a war. The Munich Agreement of 1938 is the most famous example. Many historians now think giving in did not stop the war.
fact: Appease comes from an old word meaning to bring peace, and it is related to the word peace.
fact: «Appease» means to calm someone, or stop them being angry, by giving them what they want.
fact: «Appease hunger» means to satisfy it. This is a formal use: «She ate soup to appease her hunger.»
fact: In history, appeasement means giving in to an aggressive country's demands to avoid war.
fact: Appease is a verb: appease, appeases, appeased, appeasing.
exercise: «Ella ate soup to appease her hunger.» Find and copy the word that means satisfy. | hunger | *appease | Ella | soup
exercise: «The toddler stopped crying when Mum gave him his teddy, so she appeased him.» What does appeased mean here? | *Calmed by giving him what he wanted | Shouted at until he stopped | Lost in the park | Put to bed early
exercise: Sam says appease means the same as ignore. Why is he wrong? | Appease means shouting at someone | *Appease means giving someone what they want to calm them, not ignoring them | Appease means forgetting something | Appease means ignoring someone completely
test:
«Mum appeased the crying baby with a warm bottle.» What does appeased mean? | Made angry | Woken up | *Calmed by giving what was wanted | Washed
In history, what did leaders who appeased an aggressive country do? | Declared war at once | *Gave in to its demands to avoid war | Ignored its demands completely | Sent it a letter of thanks
exam:
Which sentence uses appease correctly? | *She gave her brother the last biscuit to appease him. | She appeased the biscuit into the bin. | The biscuit appeased its way to the table. | He appeased very quickly the garden.
